## Why This Is Asked

Tests stateful per-key windowing, dynamic rule handling, and exactly-once guarantees under late messages.

## Key Concepts
- Per-account sliding window sums
- Dynamic rule lookup and on-the-fly threshold changes
- Watermarks for late arrivals and eviction
- Exactly-once semantics and idempotent fraud_alerts
- Backpressure and test canary design

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: per-account rolling sum with 5m sliding window
state = Map(); // accountId -> [{ts, amt}]
rules = Map(); // accountId -> threshold
onEvent(tx) {
  cleanExpired(tx.ts);
  sum = sumAmt(state.get(tx.accountId));
  threshold = rules.get(tx.accountId) ?? default;
  if (sum > threshold) emitFraud(tx.accountId, sum, threshold);
  append(state, tx.accountId, {ts: tx.ts, amt: tx.amount});
}
```

